      <h2 id="buying-guide">Buying Guide: Match Your Team &amp; Workflow</h2>
      <p>Do not migrate away from Salesforce on per-seat price alone. Match your primary revenue model and stack:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Growth companies marketing + sales unified &lt;200 people</strong> → HubSpot CRM. Use Free tier first, move to Starter as your leads pipeline and then Professional team marketing automation. This is the most common switch path.</li>
        <li><strong>Sales-only SMB (5–50 sellers) pure AE / SDR team</strong> → Pipedrive Professional. It's the closest thing to a spreadsheet-that-already-works: pipeline movement is the main event.</li>
        <li><strong>Support + Sales equal weight customer-first org</strong> → Freshsales Suite (CRM + Freshdesk). Consolidate your Salesforce + Zendesk spend while keeping support quality.</li>
        <li><strong>Value-first team that runs on apps everywhere (finance, HR, a full suite)</strong> → Zoho CRM (or Zoho One at 30+ users). The single-vendor breadth saves the 6-app SMB stack.</li>
        <li><strong>Project-sales overlap, custom workflow or custom visual boards PM &amp; AE working</strong> → Monday Sales CRM. When the work after the close is the bottleneck, Monday handles both side.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Common mistake: don't under-budget migration effort. 50-person implementation plan 4–8 weeks data + data dedupe + training + reps re-migration from Salesforce and marketing integrations; not + Zapier/Make. Salesforce migration. Salesforce migrations work on average 4+ weeks when account is migrated correctly.</p>
